253
00:14:48,380 --> 00:14:51,260
Sorry, but I have no
idea who you are. Hey!

254
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:53,960
Wait, hold on!

255
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:54,910
What's happening?

256
00:14:54,993 --> 00:14:56,077
I didn't do anything!

257
00:14:56,160 --> 00:14:57,748
Why is my handcuff beeping?

258
00:14:58,740 --> 00:14:59,660
Mine is, too!

259
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:00,861
Yeah, same here!

260
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:02,838
Hey, what the hell?

261
00:15:03,040 --> 00:15:04,477
Now everyone's cuff is beeping!

262
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:06,557
The motorbike went more
than 50 meters away!

263
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:07,470
But how?

264
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:09,211
It shouldn't be that far.

265
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:12,585
The guard isn't there anymore.

266
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:14,220
Where did he go?

267
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
The motorbike is covered in blood.

268
00:15:22,620 --> 00:15:23,450
Why, though?

269
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:25,857
I think I know why all
the cuffs keep beeping.

270
00:15:25,940 --> 00:15:27,777
It's gotta be because the
guard's body is moving

271
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:29,737
farther and farther
away from where we are.

272
00:15:29,820 --> 00:15:32,777
Could he have fallen into the
water and is being washed away?

273
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:34,457
Just find that stupid prick.

274
00:15:34,540 --> 00:15:36,557
Wherever he is, he's
more than 50 meters away.

275
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:37,581
The pain's good!

276
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:39,940
Hey, you guys!

277
00:15:40,380 --> 00:15:41,380
This is bad!

278
00:15:41,580 --> 00:15:43,227
Mine is getting really fast!

279
00:15:47,620 --> 00:15:48,720
There's no way!

280
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:53,780
She's dead.

281
00:15:54,220 --> 00:15:57,680
Could it be the additional
person decided to attack?

282
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:02,597
Is it because we got too close to those
discs hidden away in the storehouse?

283
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:06,680
Look 50 meters in the opposite
direction from the girl that blew up.

284
00:16:08,380 --> 00:16:09,321
He's over there!

285
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:11,937
Let's get to the guard, hurry!

286
00:16:12,020 --> 00:16:15,537
If we're close to him, this beeping
will stop and we won't explode too!

287
00:16:15,620 --> 00:16:17,257
Hey, watch your back, Jolene.

288
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:22,281
No doubt the enemy has got to be one of
those three girls and an enraged psychopath.

289
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:24,977
Personally, I already know
who I'm suspicious of.

290
00:16:25,060 --> 00:16:26,597
I bet it's that chick with the undercut.

291
00:16:26,680 --> 00:16:30,337
I mean, the girl who blew up did
say she didn't know who she was.

292
00:16:30,420 --> 00:16:32,297
It's gotta be her, I'm telling you!

293
00:16:32,380 --> 00:16:34,157
She used her stand to take out the guard!

294
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:36,597
And before she kills us,
we gotta get the bitch!

295
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:38,151
Hold on a second, Hermes.

296
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:41,157
Let's say our culprit
is who you think it is.

297
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,534
If that were the case,

298
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:44,537
doesn't that mean she would
have been guarding the

299
00:16:44,620 --> 00:16:47,157
discs in that storehouse
since before we showed up?

300
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:49,457
Yeah, I guess that's just about right.

301
00:16:49,540 --> 00:16:50,757
But that's impossible.

302
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:52,193
She's still a prisoner.

303
00:16:52,380 --> 00:16:55,615
And there's no way a prisoner
can guard something 24-7.

304
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:03,800
Joanne, stand back!

305
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:05,077
Something is in there!

306
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:05,990
What?

307
00:17:06,073 --> 00:17:06,903
Where?

308
00:17:06,986 --> 00:17:07,816
Stay the hell away from the water!

309
00:17:07,899 --> 00:17:09,581
There's something in this bucket!

310
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:16,940
Hermes, hey, did you
really see something? No.

311
00:17:20,460 --> 00:17:21,840
I guess it was nothing.

312
00:17:22,380 --> 00:17:25,498
But still, I won't be going
in this marsh ever again.

313
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:27,300
Stay close, Jolene.

314
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:30,157
The last thing we need is to
get separated from each other.

315
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:32,837
Especially since we have
no idea who the enemy is.

316
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:33,750
You're right.

317
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:36,757
And we've still got these
troublesome handcuffs to deal with.

318
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:39,177
In order to take the
discs from the storehouse,

319
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:41,457
we have to make sure we
stay within 50 meters of

320
00:17:41,540 --> 00:17:44,305
the guard's body and the
three other prisoners.

321
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:50,590
Hermes!

322
00:17:55,580 --> 00:17:57,237
What the shit was in that bucket?

323
00:17:57,320 --> 00:17:59,320
It grabbed my face out of nowhere!

324
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:03,400
What is that thing?

325
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:05,460
Some kind of demented flea?

326
00:18:08,620 --> 00:18:09,920
It split in two!

327
00:18:11,240 --> 00:18:12,960
No, now there's four of them!

328
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:14,680
What are they?

329
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:20,437
It was stupid to think that there
wasn't anything in the bucket.

330
00:18:20,520 --> 00:18:22,297
If i'd taken a second
to look more carefully,

331
00:18:22,380 --> 00:18:24,137
i'd have seen that there were
countless little bastards?

332
00:18:24,220 --> 00:18:25,808
It's swimming in the water!

333
00:18:33,260 --> 00:18:34,090
Back!

334
00:18:38,620 --> 00:18:39,620
Hermes, you're...

335
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:41,700
Jolene, stay away!

336
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:45,137
This water is a death trap and it's
getting deadlier by the second!

337
00:18:45,220 --> 00:18:48,277
I don't know how, but the
stand multiplies in the water!

338
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:49,301
Get out of here!

339
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:50,560
You can't catch up!

340
00:18:50,860 --> 00:18:53,036
This is all part of the stand's plan!

341
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,240
Stone Ocean!

342
00:19:04,820 --> 00:19:06,408
Don't worry, I'll save you!

343
00:19:09,260 --> 00:19:11,700
Jolene, she's walking on woven threads?

344
00:19:12,700 --> 00:19:16,337
But if you're using that much thread,
doesn't that mean you're losing body mass?

345
00:19:16,420 --> 00:19:18,517
every time you take a step over here?

346
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:20,600
Jolene, just get out of the water!

347
00:19:20,780 --> 00:19:23,074
Save yourself, I can take care of this!

348
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:25,590
Ah, Ura!

349
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:35,030
Impossible!

350
00:19:37,740 --> 00:19:39,060
Yes, that's right.

351
00:19:39,440 --> 00:19:41,460
It definitely feels impossible.

352
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:43,800
Good freaking grief.

353
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:48,849
If I hadn't taken out all of that thread
from my body, I'd be dead right now.

354
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:50,580
This thing's power.

355
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,824
Her guts are completely hollow.

356
00:19:53,380 --> 00:19:56,851
Oh, she let that thing hit her
so she could grab it's hand!

357
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:07,317
Jolene, we have to hurry
and get out of the water!

358
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:09,360
Don't stand up just yet, Hermes!

359
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:13,737
That parasitic fuck is really just a
bunch of tiny stands clustered together!

360
00:20:13,820 --> 00:20:16,157
They were hiding in the
water of the bucket I kicked.

361
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:18,477
Then when I turned around,
they dragged me in!

362
00:20:18,560 --> 00:20:19,619
I understand that.

363
00:20:19,780 --> 00:20:21,697
That's why I'm asking you not to stand up.

364
00:20:21,780 --> 00:20:24,440
You gotta grab onto it under the water!

365
00:20:24,860 --> 00:20:26,625
The thread that I'm releasing!

366
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:39,180
It's quick!

367
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:41,618
Powerful too, but the speed's crazy!

368
00:20:44,540 --> 00:20:46,200
What the hell is that thing?

369
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:51,324
As the stand moves farther away from its
user, it should become weaker and slower!

370
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:53,110
Son of a...

371
00:20:53,193 --> 00:20:54,420
Calm down, Jolene.

372
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:56,661
I gave our pursuer here a stigma.

373
00:20:57,200 --> 00:21:00,537
I managed to slap one on it
when I was caught in its arms.

374
00:21:00,620 --> 00:21:02,326
This is what my stand can do.

375
00:21:02,560 --> 00:21:03,760
I'll rip it off now!

376
00:21:15,460 --> 00:21:16,420
Get back!

377
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:17,896
Away from the water!

378
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:33,069
It's not coming onto land.

379
00:21:33,220 --> 00:21:36,817
As I thought, it can only attack when
its prey is in the water with it.

380
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:37,920
Please respond!

381
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:41,600
This is prisoner number FE-32125!

382
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:43,099
It's an emergency!

383
00:21:43,500 --> 00:21:45,324
The guard got into an accident!

384
00:21:45,540 --> 00:21:48,011
Somebody please just hurry up and help us!

385
00:21:48,220 --> 00:21:50,417
What the hell is going
on with the two of you?

386
00:21:50,500 --> 00:21:53,497
It almost looked as though you were
running on top of the water earlier.

387
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:54,600
Stop right there!

388
00:21:54,900 --> 00:21:56,377
Unless you want to die, move!

389
00:21:56,460 --> 00:21:58,931
All three of you, get away from the water!

390
00:22:01,460 --> 00:22:03,557
Don't go trying to do anything funny.

391
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:06,140
The enemy here is one of you!

392
00:22:09,940 --> 00:22:12,677
If we want to grab the
discs in the storehouse,

393
00:22:12,760 --> 00:22:15,407
first we have to take
care of the stand user.

394
00:22:26,260 --> 00:22:30,140
Although you think I cope

395
00:22:31,760 --> 00:22:35,240
My head is filled with hope

396
00:22:36,760 --> 00:22:43,740
Of some place other than here

397
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:50,280
Although you think I smile

398
00:22:51,700 --> 00:22:55,320
Inside and all the while

399
00:22:57,040 --> 00:23:03,360
I'm wondering About my destiny

400
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:07,897
I'm thinking

401
00:23:07,980 --> 00:23:13,577
about Out all the

402
00:23:13,660 --> 00:23:18,437
things I'd like

403
00:23:18,520 --> 00:23:25,040
to do in my life.

404
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:31,697
I'm a dreamer,

405
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:34,397
a distant dreamer,

406
00:23:34,480 --> 00:23:38,960
dreaming for me.

407
00:23:41,740 --> 00:23:44,540
From today

408
00:24:09,140 --> 00:24:09,970
Thank you.

409
00:24:39,140 --> 00:24:39,970
Thank you.
